WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.640
This video is sponsored by
Audible.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:07.729
Listen to a free audiobook and 2 Audible Originals
with the link in the description.

00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:10.830
Singapore is not known for its subtlety.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:15.499
From the minute you land and see the world’s
tallest indoor waterfall inside the airport,

00:00:15.499 --> 00:00:20.100
you’re inundated with beautiful, clean,
and green architecture.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:25.359
The sight of extraordinary, lush buildings
is so common that it almost becomes boring.

00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:29.420
All the rest, though, pale in comparison to
one.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:35.489
What the Eiffel Tower is to Paris, or the
Opera house to Sydney, the Marina Bay Sands

00:00:35.489 --> 00:00:37.280
is to Singapore.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.620
You just can’t visit without taking a photo.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:47.120
In this one, small, resort area is the famous
Gardens By The Bay, Flower Dome, Cloud Forest,

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:53.750
outdoor event piazza, convention center, theater,
art and science museum, luxury mall, two floating

00:00:53.750 --> 00:01:00.239
crystal pavilions, and, finally, 3-tower,
55-story hotel, with the world’s highest

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:02.070
pool on top.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:08.910
Altogether, the Marina Bay Sands resort cost
$5.5 billion, making it the 5th most expensive

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:10.890
building in the world.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:16.890
Perhaps the only subtle thing about it, is,
oddly enough, also, the reason it was built:

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:17.840
the casino.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:25.560
Singapore has long been a popular destination
for tourism.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.260
Beyond its use of English - far more than
its closest competitor, Hong Kong, it’s

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:34.510
also well-known for its beauty, lack of crime,
and cleanliness.

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:38.920
As an aviation hub with one of the world’s
best airlines, it’s also cheap and easy

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:41.280
for Asian travelers to get to.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:48.830
From Bangkok, 116 US Dollars, roundtrip, on
average, and 2 hours and 15 minutes, $219

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:56.970
and 4 hours and 44 minutes from Taipei, and
$318, and 8 hours, a quick hop, relatively

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.360
speaking, from Sydney.

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:04.650
But, back in the early 2000s, Singapore found
itself losing to its many regional competitors.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:11.840
It’s share of tourism in the Asia-Pacific
region shrunk from 13.1% in 1991, to just

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:14.640
5.8% by 2004.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:20.100
This, was attributed, in part, to its lack
of natural physical attractions, a symptom

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.610
of its small size.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:29.700
Today, Singapore has only 1 of the 1,121 total
UNESCO World Heritage Sites, its Botanical

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.920
Gardens, and, at the time, none.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:39.350
Neighboring Malaysia, meanwhile, has 4, Vietnam,
8, and Thailand, 5.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:43.340
All three of which are well-known, inexpensive
destinations.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:47.940
To stay competitive and revive its national
image, the Singapore government surprised

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:54.680
everyone in 2004 when it floated the radical
idea of legalizing casinos, four decades after

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.410
making them illegal.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:03:01.319
Culturally, casino gambling was considered
destructive and fundamentally at odds with

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:06.150
the country’s very conservative mentality
and willingness to ban or regulate just about

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.620
anything.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:12.890
Social and religious groups protested, a rare
sight in authoritarian Singapore, and 30,000

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:15.560
people signed a petition in opposition.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:21.010
“Casi-No” bumper stickers could be seen
on cars and hundreds of polls, surveys, and

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:22.569
dialogues were held.

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:27.290
It soon became known that the city-state’s
then 4 million people were roughly evenly

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:32.310
divided on the issue, and calls were made
for a referendum - an indicator of how passionate

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.910
the public had become.

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:39.910
Then, in April of 2005, just 13 months later,
it was all over.

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:44.510
The government announced it would allow the
construction of not one but 2 casino resorts

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:50.430
- one in the centrally-located Marina Bay,
and the other on its southern island of Sentosa.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:55.819
For comparison, Sydney debated the merits
of opening casinos for a full 6 years.

00:03:55.819 --> 00:04:00.850
But, for the Singaporean government, this
quick, effective, and sometimes contradictory

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:02.710
decision making, is characteristic.

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:08.459
In 1987, for example, its family planning
slogan was changed from “Stop at two”

00:04:08.459 --> 00:04:11.730
directly to “Have 3 or more if you can afford
it”.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:16.680
In any case, the government had made up its
mind and began soliciting Request for Concepts

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:18.360
from interested bidders.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:23.100
Importantly, the government invented the now-popular
term “Integrated Resort” to describe a

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:28.390
single development with an attached hotel,
convention center, entertainment, theme parks,

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:32.750
luxury retail shops, fine dining, and yes,
a casino.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:37.639
This was its billion-dollar hint to bidders
- although they were interested, first and

00:04:37.639 --> 00:04:42.210
foremost, in developing one of Singapore’s
first casinos, they were to be designed as

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:45.700
iconic and symbolic national landmarks.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:51.620
Of the 19 submitted proposals, 14 were shortlisted,
and 4 continued with formal bids.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:57.870
Finally, in May 2006, the Las Vegas Sands
Corporation was selected for Marina Bay, thanks

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:01.100
to its proven success in Nevada and Macau.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:06.920
Also crucial was the architect - Israeli,
Moshe Safdie, who, at age 27, had designed

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:09.250
Montreal’s famous Habitat 67.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:14.840
Safdie’s impressive proposal for a 3-tower
block design was cleverly modeled after playing

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:15.840
cards.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.260
Each of the three towers would be composed
of two structures - one flat, and one curved

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:23.350
ten times more than the Leaning Tower of Pisa.

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:27.940
This unique concept breaks conventional rules
of architecture in that higher floors actually

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:33.590
become larger and larger, until they reach
the hotel’s three, most expensive and luxurious,

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:35.150
“Chairman Suites”.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:39.930
As if not ambitious enough, there was only
a 27-month window for construction, which

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:44.960
required a 4-day cycle, meaning an entire
floor would need to be completed every four

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.910
days to stay on track.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:51.610
The Singapore government argued that a hotel
this grand deserved an equally impressive

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:52.750
pool.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:58.490
It was decided that a three-acre, 340-meter
long park would be built on top, complete

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:03.990
with jogging paths, four swimming pools, an
observation deck, promenade, restaurants,

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:06.990
spa, and 900 species of plants.

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:11.250
Called the SkyPark, it resembled a ship sailing
above Singapore.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:15.290
Beautiful as it was, the park presented several
significant challenges.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.250
First, how to get it up.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:22.449
Ultimately, the hull was constructed on the
ground in 14 sections, then lifted into place,

00:06:22.449 --> 00:06:25.650
at a slow, safe speed of 46 feet per hour.

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:29.100
16 hours to lift each segment all the way.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:34.150
Second, as infinity pools, the water needed
to flow evenly to create the illusion of falling

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:35.360
off the top.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:42.550
This, despite the fact that the 380,000-gallon
pools also laid on top of three 55-story towers

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:47.221
which would sink over time as their foundations
shifted, each at a different rate, and all

00:06:47.221 --> 00:06:49.169
susceptible to wind.

00:06:49.169 --> 00:06:53.710
To protect against this, four joints were
placed beneath each pool, capable of moving

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:57.370
up to 500 millimeters to offset any changes.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:03.220
Getting the pool from Indiana took more than
30 cargo ships, and the park alone was, itself,

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:06.470
a $150 million project.

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:12.040
When it soft-opened in 2010, the Marina Bay
Sands was neither the world’s, nor Singapore’s

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:13.280
tallest building.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:19.290
Rather, it turns heads for somehow being somewhat
absurd, fantastic, and iconic, all at the

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:20.430
same time.

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:25.830
It’s one of those few buildings which retains
its beauty no matter the angle, vantage point,

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:27.770
or time of day.

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:31.790
Inside the hotel, visitors are greeted with
a stunning hollow atrium.

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:36.330
The pools create the sensation of swimming
on top of skyscrapers.

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:40.950
While the other side of the SkyPark offers
a view of the garden and endless flow of container

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:43.360
ships passing through the strait.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:48.750
The attached mall, with its indoor canal,
is somehow just as impressive.

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:51.550
Further south is Resorts World Sentosa.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:57.020
It features a more family-friendly environment
with an aquarium, water park, Universal Studios,

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:01.710
wax museum, hotel complex, and Singapore’s
other casino.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:06.220
Although less architecturally impressive,
Resorts World Sentosa is remarkable for its

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:08.750
sheer density of attractions.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:12.820
Unsurprisingly, both locations have been hugely
successful.

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:17.160
The Marina Bay Sands has quickly become the
world’s most profitable casino and been

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:20.240
a huge source of growth for the Singapore
economy.

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:26.240
As of 2018, the tiny city-state receives more
international visitors than New York, Dubai,

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:32.159
or Paris, and only fewer than Macau, London,
Bangkok, and Hong Kong.

00:08:32.159 --> 00:08:38.180
This was and is the best case for legalizing
casinos - here, or anywhere.

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:42.430
Proponents argue it’s “easy money” - that
there’s no faster way to create wealth out

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:43.610
of thin air.

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:50.579
Amazingly, Singapore’s two resorts contribute
between 1.5 and 2% of its entire GDP.

00:08:50.579 --> 00:08:57.050
They create an estimated 20,000 jobs directly
- in the form of dealers, inspectors, hotel

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:04.720
staff, entertainers, cashiers, slot attendants
and so on, and an additional 30-40,000, indirectly.

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:09.950
Not only do they attract more tourists, but
also higher quality - business travelers and

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:11.360
VIPs.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:16.220
On the other hand, some are skeptical of the
economic benefits, suggesting increased tax

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:21.630
revenue is offset by increased expenditures
in the form of enforcement, infrastructure,

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:26.089
and, not to be forgotten, the social costs
of casinos.

00:09:26.089 --> 00:09:31.160
While the majority of Singaporeans admit to
gambling themselves, in some form, most also

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:35.129
believe casinos are unique in the way they
encourage addiction.

00:09:35.129 --> 00:09:39.730
Their interiors are designed with the express
intent of keeping players inside as long as

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:44.850
possible, which, for a small minority, leads
to pathological behavior.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:49.910
This tiny group of people then disproportionately
cost their communities in the form of lost

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:56.230
productivity, bankruptcy, crime, welfare,
and, of course, the suffering of their families.

00:09:56.230 --> 00:10:00.699
Casinos, unlike races or cruises, are available
24/7.

00:10:00.699 --> 00:10:06.739
It’s said that a casino within 10 miles
of a person’s home leads to a 90% increase

00:10:06.739 --> 00:10:10.550
in the odds of that person becoming a pathological
gambler.

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:18.540
One 2005 study also estimated such a person
costs themselves and their community $19,711

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:20.800
on average, a year.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:24.300
Casinos also target specific culturally vulnerable
groups.

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:29.420
For instance, by adhering closely to Feng
Shui principles to play on superstition.

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:32.920
Still others, accept a combination of these
arguments.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:37.819
They argue that players will travel to wherever
gambling is available - the only question

00:10:37.819 --> 00:10:40.860
is whether to capture their spending locally.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:45.300
In the U.S., for example, states are more
likely to legalize casinos when their neighbors

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:46.779
do first.

00:10:46.779 --> 00:10:53.160
In Singapore, gamblers have always had easy
access in Malaysia, Indonesia, and on cruises.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:58.340
This was one of the primary rationales for
Singapore’s decision back in 2005 - why

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:01.550
not benefit from what’s already going to
happen?

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:05.809
But, although it would do the unthinkable
and open the door to casinos, it would do

00:11:05.809 --> 00:11:09.079
so in a uniquely Singaporean way.

00:11:09.079 --> 00:11:13.279
While every other gambling hub in the world
flaunts its casinos for all they’re worth,

00:11:13.279 --> 00:11:18.370
Singapore has been very careful to balance
profit with the attendant social costs - arguably,

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:20.290
at great expense.

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:24.649
From the very beginning, the National Development
commission stipulated the casino could not

00:11:24.649 --> 00:11:28.879
occupy more than 3-5% of the total resort
space.

00:11:28.879 --> 00:11:33.309
The original plan for a strong Venetian theme
and monorail connecting the casino to the

00:11:33.309 --> 00:11:38.119
ferry terminal were later replaced, at the
insistence of the government, with the SkyPark

00:11:38.119 --> 00:11:39.220
and pool.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:44.050
The resort is also the company’s only property
where the location precedes the “Sands”

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:48.509
brand in its name - a subtle reflection of
the projects’ focus.

00:11:48.509 --> 00:11:53.299
The original architect, an expert in casino
design, was later replaced with Safdie, who

00:11:53.299 --> 00:11:56.709
was instead known for impressive and unique
architecture.

00:11:56.709 --> 00:12:01.689
The two gaps between the building’s three
towers grant a view of the sea beyond it.

00:12:01.689 --> 00:12:07.699
It complements rather than intrudes on the
skyline, in contrast to most casinos.

00:12:07.699 --> 00:12:13.529
In practice, this means the Marina Bay Sands
is neither as tacky as Vegas or shady as Macau.

00:12:13.529 --> 00:12:17.170
It’s an immediate, iconic, symbol of Singapore.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:22.500
You might spend hours shopping, eating, swimming,
even stay at the hotel, but aside for the

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:26.759
occasional sign, you may not even notice the
existence of the casino - where the company

00:12:26.759 --> 00:12:30.019
makes roughly 70% of its profit.

00:12:30.019 --> 00:12:35.699
For its part, the government has also taken
tangible steps to reduce problematic behavior.

00:12:35.699 --> 00:12:40.190
Family members can request their loved ones
be barred from gambling, those under 21 are

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:46.160
forbidden from entering casinos, and ATMs
are not available inside the gambling areas.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:52.369
Most significantly, Singapore residents are
required to pay an entry fee of $150 or $3,000

00:12:52.369 --> 00:12:57.670
per year to access each resort - neither of
which are allowed to refund or reimburse that

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:58.670
fee.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:04.069
Today, ten years after their grand openings,
most people would say Singapore has succeeded

00:13:04.069 --> 00:13:09.430
- it’s reaped the economic benefits while,
at the same time, managing the effects.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:16.220
Still, in hiding its casinos, it runs the
risk of also hiding their damage, their casualties,

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:17.559
their hardships.

00:13:17.559 --> 00:13:23.199
By taxing dubious behavior, Singapore not
only deters it and profits from it, but also

00:13:23.199 --> 00:13:26.670
risks economically depending on it.

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:32.930
After Singapore is sanitized, making itself
clean, green, and its vices, unseen, it’s

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:36.129
easy to forget what’s lost.

00:13:36.129 --> 00:13:41.239
If casinos, economics, and the economics of
casinos interest you, you’re going to love

00:13:41.239 --> 00:13:44.989
my upcoming 30-minute documentary about a
very related topic.

00:13:44.989 --> 00:13:49.879
I’ve been saying this for a while, but this
time, I promise, it’s written, recorded,

00:13:49.879 --> 00:13:51.540
and coming quite soon.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:55.970
In the meantime, you should listen to the
also related story of how two mathematicians

00:13:55.970 --> 00:14:00.790
applied their genius to the game of blackjack,
and then used their knowledge to win on wall

00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:01.790
street.

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:06.009
This story, called “Fortune’s Formula”
has just about everything that interests me:

00:14:06.009 --> 00:14:10.920
economics, business, finance, and a fascinating
narrative, and you can listen to it, along

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:14.249
with thousands of other audiobooks, with Audible.

